{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHeckeRootsForceTwist"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.jmSingleCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.jmSingleCell","kind":"instance","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.lean#L207-L227","doc":"**The hypothesis is satisfiable.**  On the one-cell diagram `λ = (1)` the JM product is `q⁰ = 1`,\nand the class instance exists with scalar `1`.  Together with `jm_scalar_unique` this shows the\nclass is a genuine constraint: inhabited, but only at the right value.\n\nThis is a consistency witness, not evidence for the general spectrum -- see the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.cells_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.cells_one","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.lean#L204-L205","doc":"The single-cell diagram has exactly one cell, `(0,0)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.jm_scalar_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.jm_scalar_unique","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.lean#L197-L202","doc":"**The hypothesis determines the scalar uniquely.**  Two instances for the same block must agree,\nbecause each forces the scalar to `θ_λ²`.  So `JucysMurphySpectrum` is not satisfiable by an\narbitrary `s` — which is what makes the conditional results above non-vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.fullTwist_single_col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.fullTwist_single_col","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.lean#L190-L193","doc":"The same check on the one-column block, whose unconditional value comes from the **sign** root. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.fullTwist_single_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.fullTwist_single_row","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.lean#L181-L188","doc":"**The conditional general result reproduces the unconditional one-row answer.**\n\nOn `λ = [n]` the Hecke-root argument already gives `θ² = q^{n(n−1)}` with no JM input\n(`theta_single_row_sq`).  The JM route must land on the same value — and does.  So the assumed\nspectrum is constrained by an independently-proved case rather than free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.fullTwist_eq_theta_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.fullTwist_eq_theta_sq","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.lean#L156-L177","doc":"**The general-`λ` twist, conditional on the Jucys–Murphy spectrum.**\n\nGiven the assumed JM spectrum, the full twist acts on `V_λ` by `θ_λ² = q^{2c(λ)}` — for **every**\npartition, not only the one-dimensional blocks.\n\nThe derivation is the unconditional part: the product of `q^{2·content}` over entries collapses to\n`q` raised to the *sum* of contents (`prod_zpow_eq_zpow_sum`), and that sum is `c(λ)` for any\ntableau (`sum_content_of_equiv`).  Neither step assumes anything about Hecke algebras.\n\n**This does not prove the general case** — it reduces it to the one named, cited hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.JucysMurphySpectrum.fullTwistScalar_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.JucysMurphySpectrum.fullTwistScalar_eq","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.lean#L153-L153","doc":"**Assumed**: the given scalar is the product of the JM eigenvalues `q^{2·content}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.JucysMurphySpectrum.tableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.JucysMurphySpectrum.tableau","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.lean#L151-L151","doc":"A standard tableau of shape `λ`, as a bijection entries ≃ cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.JucysMurphySpectrum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.JucysMurphySpectrum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.lean#L148-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.JucysMurphySpectrum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.JucysMurphySpectrum","kind":"class","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.lean#L128-L154","doc":"**The Jucys–Murphy spectrum hypothesis for the block `V_λ`.**\n\n`fullTwistScalar` is the scalar by which the central full twist `Δ²` acts on `V_λ` (Schur: it is a\nscalar because `Δ²` is central).  `tableau` is a standard tableau, as a bijection between the `n`\nentries and the cells of `λ`.\n\nThe single assumed field is `fullTwistScalar_eq`: that this scalar is the product over entries of\n`q^{2·content}`.  **This is the deep input and it is NOT proved in this corpus** — it packages the\nseminormal-form facts (JM elements act diagonally with eigenvalue `q^{2·content}`; their product\nis `Δ²`).  See the module docstring.\n\nNon-degeneracy (§3b-cond item 5).  `fullTwistScalar` is a **parameter**, not a field: it is\nsupplied by whatever exhibits the twist action, and the class *constrains* it.  An earlier draft of\nthis file made it a field, which was degenerate — the class could then be satisfied for any `λ` by\nsimply *defining* the scalar to be the product, so it constrained nothing.  As a parameter, an\ninstance exists only when the supplied scalar really is the JM product.\n\n`fullTwist_eq_theta_sq` **derives** `θ_λ²` from that hypothesis via the unconditional\ntableau-independence result — the content-sum identification is not assumed anywhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.prod_zpow_eq_zpow_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.prod_zpow_eq_zpow_sum","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.lean#L117-L124","doc":"`∏ q^{f i} = q^{∑ f i}` over a finite index set, for `q ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.card_eq_of_tableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.card_eq_of_tableau","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.lean#L112-L115","doc":"A tableau pins the entry count to the number of cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.sum_content_of_equiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.sum_content_of_equiv","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.lean#L100-L110","doc":"**The content of a tableau's entries sums to `c(λ)`, for every tableau.**\n\nA standard tableau of shape `λ` with `n` entries is in particular a bijection `Fin n ≃ cells λ`.\nSumming `content` over the entries reindexes along that bijection to a sum over the cell set, which\nis `c(λ)` by `contentSum_eq_cells_sum`.  **No Hecke hypothesis is used** — this is why the\nJucys–Murphy product is a scalar on the block rather than a per-tableau quantity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.contentSum_eq_cells_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.contentSum_eq_cells_sum","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.lean#L88-L96","doc":"**`contentSum` as a single sum over the cell set.**  Bridges the corpus's nested-`foldl`\ndefinition to a form a reindexing argument can use. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.cells_rows_disjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.cells_rows_disjoint","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.lean#L79-L86","doc":"The row-blocks of the cell set are pairwise disjoint (they differ in the row coordinate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.mem_cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.mem_cells","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.lean#L71-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.cells","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneJucysMurphyTwist.lean#L66-L69","doc":"The **cell set** of a Young diagram: `(i, j)` with `i` a row index and `j < λᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}